<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ's FCL details employee unit trust purchases.</title>
<headline>NZ's FCL details employee unit trust purchases.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fletcher Challenge Ltd on Tuesday provided further details of Employee Unit Trust (EUT) purchases and a bonus issue associated with the reorganisation of the EUT, which was announced on May 15.</p>
<p>The company will buy 36.2 million fully paid Fletcher Building shares on June 19, at market prices set on May 15.</p>
<p>It will buy 37.2 million fully paid Energy shares, 81.6 million Paper shares, and 55.7 million Forest shares, again at market prices set on May 15.</p>
<p>The bought shares would be held as treasury stock.  </p>
<p>FCL said it would issue 55.7 million Forest shares in a bonus issue. Shareholders would be entitled to four fully-paid Forest shares for every 100 shares Building, Energy or Paper shares held. The record date is June 27.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
